 "about": "Which run folder belongs to which measured platform (decision D300). The coverage matrix reads run records only through this map; a folder's name is never used to guess its platform. Keys are paths relative to a run-records root passed with --runs: 'runs/<name>' inside an assembled results directory (docs/04 section 21, scripts/assemble-results-set.ts), '<name>' in a flat folder of run folders (the matrix-set folders). Every results.json and results-advisory.json below a key belongs to the entry. Fields: platform = vti or keyring-wallet; surface = what was measured (shim, didcomm, emit, 2l, gap-shim for the wallet; agent, community, emit, 2l for VTI); checkout = the code revision the run README names, or 'not stated in the run records'; date = the run date. ceremonyRows: the ceremony rows (ceremonies/<row>/ in the results directory) with the wallet as a participant, and which wallet platform it was (null: no wallet in the row); the record's own participants must also name the keyring-wallet adapter. Ceremony outcomes are an overlay and never conformance counts. notPlatform: run folders that hold results but belong to no measured platform (the reference adapter, truststackers, the witness oracle) or that are deliberately not merged into a platform column (the wallet's witness-server surface: WIT vectors target older witness versions, decision D251). A folder with results that is in neither list is reported in the matrix limits. To add a run: add its folder here (platform, surface, checkout, date) and regenerate with npm run coverage-matrix.",
